<title>USA: N.Y. business loans fell $212 mln in May 14 week.</title>
<headline>N.Y. business loans fell $212 mln in May 14 week.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-05-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Commercial and industrial loans at the six major New York banks, excluding acceptances, fell $212 million to $45.817 billion in the week ended May 14, the Federal Reserve Bank of New York said.</p>
<p>Including acceptances, loans fell $215 million to $46.081 billion.</p>
<p>Commercial paper outstanding nationally fell $6.685 billion to $851.631 billion.</p>
<p>(( -- N.A. Treasury Desk, 212-859-1660 ))</p>
